    "title": "Mko Bazuna — Performance SLO Dashboard (PLANNED — NOT DEPLOYED)",
    "description": "PLANNED — NOT DEPLOYED (12-OPS-003). No Grafana service exists in any of the four compose files; this dashboard is a reviewable artefact for a monitoring stack a later change would deploy, and nothing consumes it today. Service-level objective monitoring for the Mko Bazuna classifieds platform. Thresholds reference the PerformanceSLO IntEnum from src/benchmark/constants.py (Block B1 deliverable).",
    "tags": ["slo", "performance", "django-prometheus", "mko-bazuna"],
    "schemaVersion": 39,
    "version": 1,
    "refresh": "30s",
    "time": {
      "from": "now-1h",
      "to": "now"
    },
    "templating": {
      "list": [
        {
          "type": "interval",
          "name": "interval",
          "label": "Resolution",
          "query": "1m,5m,15m",
          "current": {
            "text": "5m",
            "value": "5m"
          },
          "auto": false,
          "hide": 0,
          "includeLabels": false,
          "multi": false,
          "queryType": 0,
          "refresh": 2,
          "auto_count": 2,
          "sort": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    "annotations": {
      "list": [
        {
          "builtIn": 1,
          "datasource": {
            "type": "grafana",
            "uid": "-- Dashboard --"
          },
          "enable": true,
          "hide": true,
          "iconColor": "rgba(0, 211, 255, 1)",
          "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
          "target": {
            "limit": 100,
            "matchAny": [],
            "tags": []
          },
          "type": "dashboard"
        }
      ]
    },
    "panels": [
      {
        "id": "search-p95-latency",
        "type": "graph",
        "title": "Search p95 Latency (ms)",
          "description": "95th-percentile response time for the /search/ endpoint, derived from the django_http_requests_latency_including_middlewares_seconds histogram (django-prometheus). Threshold: PerformanceSLO.P95_SLO_MS = 500ms (src/benchmark/constants.py).",
        "gridPos": {
          "h": 8,
          "w": 12,
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0
        },
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "targets": [
          {
            "refId": "A",
            "datasource": {
              "type": "prometheus",
              "uid": "prometheus"
            },
              "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(django_http_requests_latency_including_middlewares_seconds_bucket{view=\"search:search\"}[$__interval]))) * 1000",
            "legendFormat": "p95 latency",
            "range": true
          }
        ],
        "fieldConfig": {
          "defaults": {
            "unit": "ms",
            "custom": {
              "drawStyle": "line",
              "lineWidth": 2,
              "fillOpacity": 10,
              "gradientMode": "none"
            },
            "thresholds": {
              "mode": "absolute",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "color": "green",
                  "value": null
                },
                {
                  "color": "red",
                  "value": 500
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "options": {
          "tooltip": {
            "mode": "single"
          },
          "legend": {
            "displayMode": "list",
            "placement": "bottom"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "search-p99-latency",
        "type": "graph",
        "title": "Search p99 Latency (ms)",
          "description": "99th-percentile response time for the /search/ endpoint, derived from the django_http_requests_latency_including_middlewares_seconds histogram (django-prometheus). Threshold: PerformanceSLO.SEARCH_SLO_MS = 2000ms (src/benchmark/constants.py; docs/01-spec/search-patterns.md:360).",
        "gridPos": {
          "h": 8,
          "w": 12,
          "x": 12,
          "y": 0
        },
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "targets": [
          {
            "refId": "A",
            "datasource": {
              "type": "prometheus",
              "uid": "prometheus"
            },
              "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(django_http_requests_latency_including_middlewares_seconds_bucket{view=\"search:search\"}[$__interval]))) * 1000",
            "legendFormat": "p99 latency",
            "range": true
          }
        ],
        "fieldConfig": {
          "defaults": {
            "unit": "ms",
            "custom": {
              "drawStyle": "line",
              "lineWidth": 2,
              "fillOpacity": 10,
              "gradientMode": "none"
            },
            "thresholds": {
              "mode": "absolute",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "color": "green",
                  "value": null
                },
                {
                  "color": "orange",
                  "value": 1000
                },
                {
                  "color": "red",
                  "value": 2000
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "options": {
          "tooltip": {
            "mode": "single"
          },
          "legend": {
            "displayMode": "list",
            "placement": "bottom"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "redis-cache-hit-rate",
        "type": "gauge",
        "title": "Redis Cache Hit Rate (%) — NOT AVAILABLE",
        "description": "NOT AVAILABLE (12-OPS-003): this panel reads Redis keyspace hits/misses from a redis_exporter. No redis_exporter exists in any of the four compose files, so the series is never exposed. The panel is retained only as a placeholder and does not read as an active control. Threshold when a exporter is deployed: PerformanceSLO.CACHE_HIT_RATE_THRESHOLD = 85% (src/benchmark/constants.py; docs/99-agent/rules.md:221).",
        "gridPos": {
          "h": 8,
          "w": 8,
          "x": 0,
          "y": 8
        },
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "targets": [
          {
            "refId": "A",
            "datasource": {
              "type": "prometheus",
              "uid": "prometheus"
            },
            "expr": "100 * sum(rate(redis_db_keyspace_hits_total[1m])) / (sum(rate(redis_db_keyspace_hits_total[1m])) + sum(rate(redis_db_keyspace_misses_total[1m]))",
            "legendFormat": "hit rate",
            "range": true
          }
        ],
        "fieldConfig": {
          "defaults": {
            "unit": "percent",
            "min": 0,
            "max": 100,
            "thresholds": {
              "mode": "absolute",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "color": "green",
                  "value": null
                },
                {
                  "color": "orange",
                  "value": 85
                },
                {
                  "color": "red",
                  "value": 85
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "options": {
          "reduceOptions": {
            "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
            "fields": "",
            "values": false
          },
          "orientation": "horizontal",
          "textMode": "value"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "error-rate-5xx",
        "type": "graph",
        "title": "Error Rate (5xx) — Burn Rate",
          "description": "NOTE (12-OPS-003): the default django-prometheus exposition exposes NO status-code-labelled counter, so a true 5xx panel is not expressible without a custom metric. This panel shows the total response rate (django_http_responses_before_middlewares_total) as a proxy and is a placeholder for a stack a later change would deploy.",
        "gridPos": {
          "h": 8,
          "w": 8,
          "x": 8,
          "y": 8
        },
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "targets": [
          {
            "refId": "A",
            "datasource": {
              "type": "prometheus",
              "uid": "prometheus"
            },
            "expr": "sum by (method) (rate(django_http_responses_before_middlewares_total[5m]))",
            "legendFormat": "{{method}}",
            "range": true
          }
        ],
        "fieldConfig": {
          "defaults": {
            "unit": "short",
            "custom": {
              "drawStyle": "line",
              "lineWidth": 2,
              "fillOpacity": 20,
              "gradientMode": "none"
            },
            "thresholds": {
              "mode": "absolute",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "color": "green",
                  "value": null
                },
                {
                  "color": "red",
                  "value": 1
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "options": {
          "tooltip": {
            "mode": "single"
          },
          "legend": {
            "displayMode": "list",
            "placement": "bottom"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "slo-budget-burn-rate",
        "type": "stat",
        "title": "Search SLO Error Budget Remaining",
        "description": "Remaining percentage of the search latency error budget (99% SLO — 1% budget). When this drops below 90%, the search_slo_burn_rate alert fires. See prometheus-slo-alerts.yaml.",
        "gridPos": {
          "h": 4,
          "w": 4,
          "x": 16,
          "y": 8
        },
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "targets": [
          {
            "refId": "A",
            "datasource": {
              "type": "prometheus",
              "uid": "prometheus"
            },
            "expr": "100 * (1 - (1 - rate(django_http_requests_latency_including_middlewares_seconds_bucket{le=\"2.5\", view=\"search:search\"}[1h]) / rate(django_http_requests_latency_including_middlewares_seconds_count{view=\"search:search\"}[1h])) / 0.01)",
            "legendFormat": "budget remaining",
            "range": true
          }
        ],
        "fieldConfig": {
          "defaults": {
            "unit": "percent",
            "min": 0,
            "max": 100,
            "thresholds": {
              "mode": "absolute",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "color": "orange",
                  "value": 0
                },
                {
                  "color": "green",
                  "value": 10
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "options": {
          "colorMode": "value",
          "graphMode": "none",
          "justifyMode": "auto",
          "textMode": "auto",
          "reduceOptions": {
            "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
            "fields": "",
            "values": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "known-limitation-panel",
        "type": "text",
        "title": "Metrics Mode — Multiprocess Aggregation",
        "gridPos": {
          "h": 4,
          "w": 24,
          "x": 0,
          "y": 12
        },
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "targets": [],
        "fieldConfig": {
          "defaults": {}
        },
        "options": {
          "content": "<div style=\"color: #0b6e4f; font-weight: bold;\">\n<h3>Multiprocess Metrics Mode (12-OPS-003)</h3>\n<p>\nThe application runs gunicorn with <code>preload_app=True</code>, but the web service sets\n<code>PROMETHEUS_MULTIPROC_DIR</code> (with a paired tmpfs) and <code>gunicorn.conf.py</code>\ndefines the <code>child_exit</code> hook calling\n<code>prometheus_client.multiprocess.mark_process_dead(worker.pid)</code>, so\n<code>prometheus_client</code> runs in <strong>multiprocess mode</strong> and a single\n<code>/metrics</code> scrape aggregates every worker's metrics. The earlier caveat that one\nscrape returned only one worker's metrics no longer holds.\n</p>\n<p>\nThe <code>/metrics</code> endpoint is restricted to loopback via nginx\n(<code>allow 127.0.0.1; deny all;</code>) and again in Django\n(<code>config/urls.py</code>), so a scraper must run on the same host or behind a proxy that\nis deliberately widened. No Prometheus or Grafana service is deployed today.\n</p>\n</div>",
          "mode": "html"
        }
      }
    ],
